 &lt;BR&gt; 
3. The Board of Directors of the Company, at its meeting held on 29th June, 2024, approved the &lt;BR&gt; 
issuance of equity shares by way of Qualified Institutional Placement for a maximum amount of                              Rs.750 crores. Subsequently, the Fund-Raising Committee of the Board of Directors of the Company, &lt;BR&gt; 
at its meeting held on 11th July, 2025, approved the allotment of 16,02,564 equity shares of face &lt;BR&gt; 
value of Rs.2/- each to eligible Investors at an issue price of Rs.4,680/- per equity share (including a &lt;BR&gt; 
premium of Rs.4,678/-per equity share), aggregating to Rs.750 crores. &lt;BR&gt; 
 &lt;BR&gt; 
4. The consolidated results include the financial results of three foreign subsidiaries – Manchester &lt;BR&gt; 
Organics Limited, NFIL (UK) Limited and Navin Fluorine (Shanghai) Co. Limited, a step-down &lt;BR&gt; 
foreign subsidiary – NFIL USA Inc., a 100% subsidiary of NFIL (UK) Limited, two Indian &lt;BR&gt; 
subsidiaries – Sulakshana Securities Limited and Navin Fluorine Advanced Sciences Limited, a joint &lt;BR&gt; 
venture company – Swarnim Gujarat Fluorspar Private Limited. &lt;BR&gt; 
 &lt;BR&gt; 
